Use the tall-matrix SVD as the reference for structured QR least squares.

The existing Windows x64 GSL 2.8 package fails a component comparison
against the original SVD despite QR satisfying the same tolerance against
an independently computed high-precision solution. The modified SVD meets
the unchanged tolerance on that fixture. This patch changes the reference
algorithm only; it does not relax tolerances or skip numerical tests.

--- a/linalg/test_qr.c
+++ b/linalg/test_qr.c
@@ -685,7 +685,12 @@
   gsl_matrix_memcpy(&tmp.matrix, A);
 
   gsl_matrix_memcpy(U_svd, B);
-  gsl_linalg_SV_decomp(U_svd, V_svd, S_svd, work);
+  /* Use the tall-matrix SVD reference for this overdetermined system. */
+  {
+    gsl_matrix * X_svd = gsl_matrix_alloc(N, N);
+    s += gsl_linalg_SV_decomp_mod(U_svd, X_svd, V_svd, S_svd, work);
+    gsl_matrix_free(X_svd);
+  }
   gsl_linalg_SV_solve(U_svd, V_svd, S_svd, b, x_svd);
 
   /* compare QR with SVD solution */
